<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    ⛔ updatePeriodMillis="0" — the widget polls NOTHING, and never may. Any other value asks the
    system to wake this app on a timer (30 minutes at the very least, whether or not a single
    message moved) to redraw a number that has not changed. The widget is redrawn when the system
    asks: when it is placed, after a reboot and after an app update — and, since UnreadWidgetPush
    was wired into SternaApplication, whenever the count itself moves. That collector is the reason
    this attribute stays 0 rather than the reason it might one day change: it pushes on a number
    that actually moved, which a timer cannot do.

    resizeMode lets the cell be dragged to any size, and that is not decorative either: past a size
    it draws a line per account instead of one figure, and the LAUNCHER picks between the two from
    the RemoteViews size map UnreadWidgetDraw hands it. Nothing here declares that threshold, and
    nothing reads OPTION_APPWIDGET_MIN_*/MAX_* to find it — those four numbers describe two
    orientations rather than one size. Android 12 and up only; below it the cell keeps
    @layout/widget_unread at every size.

    android:description and android:previewLayout are API 31+, so they live in res/xml-v31 rather
    than under a tools:targetApi here. Below API 31 the picker falls back to the app's icon and
    shows no description: less pretty, and nothing else.
-->
<appwidget-provider xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:initialLayout="@layout/widget_unread"
    android:minHeight="40dp"
    android:minWidth="110dp"
    android:resizeMode="horizontal|vertical"
    android:updatePeriodMillis="0"
    android:widgetCategory="home_screen" />
